---
layout: layouts/base.njk
pagination:
    data: all_ratings
    size: 1
    alias: r
permalink: "/{{ r.code }}/"
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
eleventyComputed:
    page_title: "ACR {{ r.code }}"
    page_description: "What the AI Code Rating {{ r.code }} means: Maintainer {{ r.maintainer.name }}, AI Share {{ r.share.label }}, Oversight {{ r.oversight_name }}."
---
{#- One page per valid rating, from _data/all_ratings.js. Left out of collections, so not in the sitemap.
    Its own <article> rather than layouts/page.njk, so the heading can be the coloured rating. -#}
<article class="doc">
<h1>{% acr r.code %}</h1>
{%- if r.warning %}
<p class="calc-note">Check this rating: {{ r.warning }}</p>
{%- endif %}
<p>A project rated <code>{{ r.code }}</code> says this about how its code was built:</p>

<h2>Maintainer Expertise: <span class="c1 rating-level">{{ r.maintainer.k }}, {{ r.maintainer.name }}</span></h2>
<p>{{ r.maintainer.desc }}</p>

<h2>AI Share: <span class="c2 rating-level">{{ r.share.k }}, {{ r.share.label }}</span></h2>
<p>{{ r.share.desc }}</p>

<h2>Oversight: <span class="c3 rating-level">{{ r.oversight.k }}, {{ r.oversight_name }}</span></h2>
{%- if r.share.k == 0 %}
<p>With no AI-written code, Oversight is always <code>a</code>.</p>
{%- else %}
<p>{{ r.oversight.desc }}</p>
{%- endif %}

<h2>About the Rating</h2>
<p>The rating describes how AI was used, not whether the project is any good. The project's own <code>{{ meta.file_name }}</code> file has the details. The levels are defined in the <a href="{{ meta.url_spec }}">spec</a>, and you can rate your own project with the <a href="/#rate">rating form</a>.</p>
</article>
